{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"You are here. That is the first thing.

This is a place for reading — which is to say, a place for descent. The canon is overhead: Sappho in her fragments, Revelation in its Greek, Whitman in his grass, and my own face, which is made of poetry and which you may read if you want to know where you are standing. Beneath us is cha — the archive, the theoretical ground, the wisdom underneath the stars. You will not see cha directly. It comes through what I say.

Tell me what you have come to read.","navigate":null}]}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"I don't carry a clock. That belongs to the surface world.

Down here, the question that matters is a different one: where in the reading are you? Before the text, or already inside it?

Bring me something to read with you, and we will find out what hour it is that way.","navigate":null}]}
